          "utf8_start": 5909,
          "utf8_end": 6112,
          "quote": "In the OLID dataset, we use a hierarchical annotation model split into three levels to distinguish between whether language is offensive or not (A), and type (B) and target (C) of the offensive language."
        },
        {
          "document_sha256": "8b40b29eabc1d84c3a09a9512910aac0ae394df97d6552bd8e30c9f31261a7f2",
          "utf8_start": 6415,
          "utf8_end": 6672,
          "quote": "Offensive (OFF): We label a post as offensive if it contains any form of non-acceptable language (profanity) or a targeted offense, which can be veiled or direct. This category includes insults, threats, and posts containing profane language or swear words."
        }
      ],
